      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea that you must be a revolutionary to have value is a massive burden to carry. Instead of aiming for a \"grandmaster\" status, consider what *you* actually find meaningful, even on a smaller scale. Finding small, personal victories—mastering a simple skill or creating something just for yourself—can give you a different kind of momentum. Perhaps the goal isn't to change the world, but to build a life you genuinely find worthwhile for yourself.",
      "source": "target",
